      "header": "Metacognitive Prospective Memory Inventory – Short Version (MPMI-s) Report",
      "footer_refs": [
        "Rummel, J., Danner, D., & Kuhlmann, B. G. (2019). The short version of the Metacognitive Prospective Memory Inventory (MPMI-s): Factor structure, reliability, validity, and reference data. Measurement Instruments for the Social Sciences, 1, Article e10999. https://doi.org/10.1186/s42409-019-0008-6",
        "Higher PMA scores indicate better prospective memory abilities. Higher PMSi and PMSe scores indicate more frequent strategy use."
