  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "mpmi_r1": "Rarely",
      "mpmi_r2": "Rather rarely",
      "mpmi_r3": "Sometimes",
      "mpmi_r4": "Rather often",
      "mpmi_r5": "Often",
      "instructions": "Please indicate how often each of the following statements applies to you.",
      "pma1": "I forget to cancel contracts on time, like trial subscriptions for newspapers.",
      "pma2": "I remember to run errands that need to be completed within a specific timeframe, like picking up my laundry from the dry cleaner before it closes.",
      "pma3": "If I've borrowed something from someone for a while, I remember to give it back to that person the next time we see each other.",
      "pma4": "I forget to call a friend again after I could not reach him or her on the first try.",
      "pma5": "I receive overdue notifications because I forget to pay bills on time.",
      "pma6": "I am able to remind myself of phone calls I need to make, such as calling a friend on his or her birthday.",
      "pma7": "I remember my appointments which are coming up in a few days without writing them down.",
      "pma8": "I do not send e-mails or letters on time, even when I wrote myself a reminder to do so.",
      "pmsi1": "Even when I'm busy doing other things, I deliberately try to keep unfinished tasks in mind so that I do not forget them.",
      "pmsi2": "In the morning, I go through the day's tasks in my head so that I do not forget to remember something.",
      "pmsi3": "When I have to complete steps in a specific order, such as when I am baking, I visualize the sequence of steps before starting.",
      "pmsi4": "After completing a task, I check once again whether I took care of everything, like turning off the stove after cooking.",
      "pmsi5": "In my mind, I make a list of things that I still have to complete.",
      "pmsi6": "I think of my to-do list while I am busy doing something else, like washing dishes or working out.",
      "pmsi7": "Before I go shopping, I picture where the products I need are located in the store, so that I do not forget to pick them up when I walk through the aisles.",
      "pmse1": "I write myself a to-do list to remind me of things that I still need to accomplish.",
      "pmse2": "I write shopping lists.",
      "pmse3": "When I have to take something with me the next morning, like a letter or a library book, I put it in my bag the evening before so that I will not forget it the next day.",
      "pmse4": "I keep a calendar with all of my appointments.",
      "pmse5": "To help me remember to do things, I stick \"Post-it\" notes in obvious places.",
      "pmse6": "If I put things in particular places so that I'm reminded of tasks I need to do (for example, putting a full trash bag in front of the door so I do not forget to take it out).",
      "pmse7": "For things that I need to do on a regular basis, I plan to do them at the same time each day (for example, always taking my medication in the evening before brushing my teeth).",
      "debrief": "Thank you for completing this questionnaire."
    }
  }
}